<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/telecom">Telecommunications</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">RF &amp; High-Frequency Assembly</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Telecommunications products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s active" href="/markets/telecom/rf-assembly"><span class="abbr">RF</span><span class="label">RF &amp; High-Frequency Assembly</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us the frequency band and the package and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Telecommunications &middot; RF &amp; High-Frequency Assembly</div><h1 class="mk-h1">RF and high-frequency assembly for telecom</h1><p class="mk-lede">At RF, microwave and millimeter-wave frequencies the assembly sits inside the electrical result. Die placement, the void content of an attach layer, ground-path continuity and the integrity of a seal are all part of the circuit, which is why high-frequency work has to be measured rather than inspected.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-rf-assembly" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ RF &amp; High-Frequency Assembly &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-rf-assembly" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hana assembles RF and microwave modules, millimeter-wave modules, RF power amplifiers and fiber-optic components, and verifies them on rack-and-stack RF instrumentation — spectrum analyzer, network analyzer and noise figure — rather than a pass/fail buzz. This is work Hana has been doing for decades; the same optical and high-frequency base later fed our <a href="markets-data-centers.html">data-center</a> programs.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">RF and microwave modules</span></div><div class="desc">module-level assembly with controlled ground paths and shielding, built and RF-measured before shipment.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Millimeter-wave modules</span></div><div class="desc">mmWave module assembly on lines that already run high-frequency programs.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">RF power amplifier assembly</span></div><div class="desc">GaN-on-Si die into TO-272 plastic and metal-ceramic packages, with AuSn eutectic or sintered die attach, multi-die module build and ceramic lid encapsulation.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Fiber-optic components</span></div><div class="desc">optical component assembly, with hermetic sealing and helium fine-leak test available where the package calls for it.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Process depth sits on the capability page: System in Package owns the wider multi-die integration range these modules sit inside, together with the wafer-level steps and final test either side of assembly.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/osat/flip-chip-sip">Explore System in Package <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Die attach, sealing and real RF measurement</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">In an RF module the layer under the die is a thermal and electrical path, not an adhesive — so Hana selects the attach method to the package rather than to a default. AuSn eutectic where a void-free, high-conductivity bond line is called for; sintered attach where the thermal path has to be shorter still. Die go into TO-272 plastic and metal-ceramic packages, multi-die modules are built and bonded as one assembly, and the package is closed with a ceramic lid or a hermetic seal, with helium fine-leak test available to verify it. Then the module is measured, not buzzed: rack-and-stack RF test with spectrum and network analyzers and noise-figure measurement, against the requirements set for the program.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ayutthaya"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div><div class="note">microwave and fiber-optic components, SiP and SMT</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">millimeter-wave modules</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Why does assembly matter more at high frequency?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Because at RF and above the build becomes part of the circuit. Ground-path continuity, shielding, the void content of a die-attach layer and the integrity of a seal all sit inside the electrical result, so they have to be controlled as process steps and then confirmed by measurement — not assumed from a visual check.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What RF products can Hana assemble?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">RF and microwave modules, millimeter-wave modules, RF power amplifiers — including GaN-on-Si die in TO-272 plastic and metal-ceramic packages, multi-die modules and ceramic lid encapsulation — and fiber-optic components, with hermetic sealing where the package calls for it.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How does Hana test RF assemblies before shipment?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">With rack-and-stack RF measurement: spectrum analyzer, network analyzer and noise-figure measurement, run against the requirements set for the program. Where a package is sealed, helium fine-leak test can verify the seal beforehand. The test set is selected per program and confirmed per site.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/telecom" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Telecommunications market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your RF program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>
